  "name": "Google Drive photo inbox: remove backgrounds and log results in Google Sheets with LassoCut",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "02743553-5f88-521e-ade0-cdd5eaf52a84",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -820,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 760,
        "height": 900,
        "content": "## Google Drive photo inbox: remove backgrounds and log results in Google Sheets with LassoCut\n\n### Who it's for\nE-commerce teams, photographers and marketers who drop product or portrait photos into a Google Drive folder and want clean cut-outs plus a log of what was done, without opening an image editor.\n\n### How it works\n1. **New photo in the input folder** checks the folder every minute. **Run now** lists the files already there, so you can process a backlog.\n2. **Keep images under 22 MB** keeps JPG, PNG and WebP files and skips anything above the API limit.\n3. **Loop over files** handles one photo at a time: download, **Remove background with LassoCut**, then **Save the cut-out** as `<name>-cutout.png` in the output folder.\n4. The original moves to the **done** folder and a row is added to your Google Sheet: date, file name, links, credits charged, width, height and detected subject type.\n5. If the download, the cut-out or the upload fails (unreadable file, no credits left...), the original moves to the **failed** folder, the error is logged and the loop goes on.\n6. **Build run summary** counts processed and failed photos and the credits used.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the verified community node **n8n-nodes-lassocut** (Settings > Community nodes).\n2. Create a free account at https://www.lassocut.com and add your API key as a **LassoCut API** credential.\n3. Add a **Google Drive OAuth2** credential on the trigger and the Drive nodes, and a **Google Sheets OAuth2** credential on **Append row to the log sheet**.\n4. Create four Drive folders (input, output, done, failed) and an empty Google Sheet with a tab named `Log` (headers are added on the first run). Paste their URLs in **Settings** and pick the same input folder in the trigger.\n5. Set **size** to `preview` for a free test, click **Run now**, then publish the workflow.\n\n### Requirements\n- Google Drive and Google Sheets.\n- A LassoCut account. Free accounts get 50 previews a month (up to 10 a day). A full-size result costs 1 credit. Credit packs start at $9 for 100 credits, and credits never expire.\n\n### How to customise\n- **Settings**: background colour (empty = transparent, `ffffff` = white), size, format (`png`, `jpg`, `webp`) and size limit.\n- Set **Subject Type** or **Crop to Subject** in the LassoCut node options.\n- Send the run summary to Slack or Gmail.\n\n### Disclosure\nBuilt by the founder of LassoCut, who maintains the n8n-nodes-lassocut node."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
